1992</year>) Plague: a clinical review of 27 cases. <source>Arch. Intern. Med.</source> <volume>152</volume>,  <fpage>1253</fpage>&#x02013;1256<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1599354</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r9"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal">Nielsen, K., Smith, P., Yu, W. L., and Halbert, G. ( <year>2007</year>) Salmonella enterica serotype urbana interference with brucellosis serology. <source>J. Immunoassay Immunochem.</source> <volume>28</volume>,  <fpage>289</fpage>&#x02013;296<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17613674</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r10"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal">Rahman, M. Z., Sultana, M., Khan, S. I., and Birkeland, N. K. ( <year>2007</year>) Serological cross-reactivity of environmental isolates of <italic>Enterobacter</italic>, <italic>Escherichia</italic>, <italic>Stenotrophomonas</italic>, and <italic>Aerococcus</italic> with <italic>Shigella</italic> spp.-specific antisera. <source>Curr. Microbiol.</source> <volume>54</volume>,  <fpage>63</fpage>&#x02013;67<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17171463</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r11"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal">Chart, H., Okubadejo, O. A., and Rowe, B. ( <year>1992</year>) The serological relationship between <italic>Escherichia coli</italic> O157 and <italic>Yersinia enterocolitica</italic> O9 using sera from patients with brucellosis. <source>Epidemiol. Infect.</source> <volume>108</volume>,  <fpage>77</fpage>&#x02013;85<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1547843</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r12"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal">McCabe, W. R., Bruins, S. C., Craven, D. E., and Johns, M. ( <year>1977</year>) Cross-reactive antigens: their potential for immunization-induced immunity to Gram-negative bacteria. <source>J. Infect. Dis.</source> <volume>136</volume>,  <fpage>(suppl.) S161</fpage>&#x02013;S166<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">330775</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r13"><label>13</label><citation citation-